From: Pley
Subject: add dovi_compose, a Dolby Vision dual-layer composer
Origin: Pley's own (deploy/ffmpeg/README.md)

Rebuilds the picture of a Dolby Vision profile 7 stream from its base
layer, its full enhancement layer and their metadata (RPU), as ETSI GS
CCM 001's composer does: polynomial and MMR mapping, linear dead zone
NLQ, and its annex B's enhancement layer resampling. The output is 12-
or 10-bit BT.2020 PQ without Dolby Vision metadata, for Pley's
experimental use of the full enhancement layer. The brightness the RPU
gives each scene (level 1) goes on as HDR10+, which tone mappers read in
its place.

Experimental: checked against an independent implementation of the
specification and Dolby Vision test vectors on synthetic streams, not
against a Dolby decoder or a real disc. GPL (--enable-gpl), under
FFmpeg's licence as the files it changes.
